note addr a1: every way the default code generator takes an address, under a position independent
note image. The texts stand before 180 filler lines (about 4 KiB of code that is never run), so each
note later use is on another 4 KiB page than the text it names and ADRP carries a page distance.
note Printed: tb read byte by byte; ta passed as a view parameter; the byte sum of ta; a global
note written and read back.
text ta "text one\n"
text tb "second text, used from a later page\n"
global gb uchar 16

